    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0230" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2021: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Military Governor of Santo Domingo</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fuller</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d75-f1"/></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-28T23:02:00-04:40"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1918, 11.02 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The following message is for the Department of State. Prospective investors in
                    1918 Dominican Bonds raise point that if $20,000,000 Bond[s] of 1908 are
                    redeemed prior to January 1938, the custom Receivership terminates &amp; 1918
                    bonds will therefore not have Amortization and interest guaranteed by U.S.
                    Collector of customs. Military Government’s interpretation of United States
                    Government’s consent issue 1918 bonds is that it constitutes an extension of
                    provision of American Dominican convention of 1918 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1907</hi>]<anchor n="23" xml:id="d75-f2"/> until both loans are fully
                    redeemed. Investors’ contentions tend to greatly reduce value of 1918 bonds.
                    Strongly recommends immediate decision <pb facs="0231" n="146" xml:id="pg146"/>
                    being given confirming military Governor’s interpretation, original publication
                    of decision in financial publication. 1918 bonds lately issued. Prestige of
                    military Government will be greatly diminished if its interpretation is not
                    upheld. Cable advices of action requested. 12028.</p>
                <closer>[No signature indicated]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
